- "One Piece" and "Naruto" and "Bleach."

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:15.840
So I love seeing everyone loving things

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:17.580
that might not necessarily be-

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:19.350
You have a lot of young girls.

00:11:19.350 --> 00:11:22.320
You have a lot of female
fans of the shonen genre.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:23.153
- Completely.

00:11:23.153 --> 00:11:24.900
- And I love that we're
seeing a lot of people

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:27.240
just embracing good stories
and good characters,

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:30.000
even if technically they're
not the target audience

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.000
for what the particular series might be.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:36.060
- But I think the categorization
of this is meant for them,

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:38.370
that is meant for this
is slowly disappearing

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:42.690
as people's likes, wants,
and needs are ever shifting.

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:47.160
And that's what's so much fun
is there needs to be no shame,

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:50.610
no need for you to feel weird
about watching something

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:53.400
that might not be meant
for you, but that's okay.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.767
Watch it anyway 'cause
it is meant for you,

00:11:54.767 --> 00:11:56.310
'cause it's meant for everyone.

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:58.050
- And so within that, one of the critiques

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:01.020
that you kind of see of
shonen more specifically

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:04.740
is they don't have good female characters.

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:05.850
Shonen series don't have

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:07.656
good female characters.
- Okay, Interesting.

00:12:07.656 --> 00:12:10.290
- Sakura from "Naruto" is a
big, she's kind of unfortunately

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:12.720
like the poster child of that idea.

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:13.740
- By the way, I agree.

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:16.050
- I agree with you also, but
the point that I'm trying

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:19.050
to make is it's not entirely true.

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:20.243
It might be situationally true.

00:12:20.243 --> 00:12:22.050
- No, of course.
- You brought Erza up before

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:25.153
who is incredible, one of
the best female characters-

00:12:25.153 --> 00:12:29.237
one of the (indistinct)
characters, period, in shonen.

00:12:29.237 --> 00:12:30.810
What are some other female characters

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:33.157
that you love from shonen series?

00:12:33.157 --> 00:12:34.347
- "Attack on Titan."

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:37.620
You have many of them. You have Sasha.

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:41.400
I mean, that show just does
characters in general, well.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:45.390
But Sasha Mikasa and Annie.

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:46.260
- Yes.

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:48.510
- It's like both, all three
of them are incredible

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:51.480
characters with their own
characteristics that I love.

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:54.600
Then you have, well, "Chainsaw Man"

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:58.410
is like the new one, right,
where you can really...

00:12:58.410 --> 00:12:59.730
- Wait. Have we talked about this yet?

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:00.930
- Oh, you think-

00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:02.460
- Are you a Power or a Makima?

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:04.110
- Can I say neither?

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:05.430
- And that ends this episode

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:07.020
of "The MANA podcast."
(Tony laughing)

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:08.352
Thanks for your time, Tony.

00:13:08.352 --> 00:13:09.690
(indistinct talking)

00:13:09.690 --> 00:13:12.360
- More power than Makima.

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:15.840
But like, Makima's just
a horrible human being

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:19.159
and it makes for an incredible
character, because again,

00:13:19.159 --> 00:13:21.540
talking about women
not being written well.

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:23.610
But here's a woman who probably

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:25.800
would've been written as a
man, but written as a woman

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:28.170
and is interesting because she's a woman.

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:30.060
Power is waifu.

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:32.280
Power is like, all right, if I'm picking

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:34.560
someone to marry here, her.

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:36.540
But I can't remember her name.

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:37.796
One eye patch.

00:13:37.796 --> 00:13:38.629
- Oh, Himeno.

00:13:38.629 --> 00:13:40.440
- Himeno. Himeno is number one for me.

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:42.550
- Yeah, we know. We do
love Himeno around here.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:44.520
- Yeah, yeah, yeah. (laughing)

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:46.485
- No, those are good choices.

00:13:46.485 --> 00:13:48.090
- Did I survive?

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:52.380
- For not just immediately
saying Power above everyone else,

00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:54.780
yeah, you did a fine job.
- Himeno's number one.

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:55.993
Then it's Power.
- I respect it.

00:13:55.993 --> 00:13:57.805
- Thank you.
- I respect it.

00:13:57.805 --> 00:13:59.760
- As long as I didn't say Makima.

00:13:59.760 --> 00:14:00.593
- And look.

00:14:00.593 --> 00:14:01.710
What I think is interesting
about that though

00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:04.551
is I don't like Makima.

00:14:04.551 --> 00:14:06.080
- Yeah.
- But it's because Makima

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:07.443
is such a good character.

00:14:07.443 --> 00:14:11.943
It's who she is and what she
does that makes me dislike her.

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:14.760
A well-written character
can be a character

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:16.620
who is hated also.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:18.660
- But I think that's the
issue is that we have

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:21.150
our own personal perceived notions.

00:14:21.150 --> 00:14:24.090
And I think even though it's
shonen and they're saying

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:27.060
shonen has a problem, it's
how we view women as well

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:29.340
that I think is a very
interesting thing, right?

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:31.290
Sometimes if you don't like a character,

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:33.450
that might be very, very intentional,

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:34.920
but you don't like her and then you go,

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:37.320
well, I hate that character
and she's written poorly

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:41.400
because we expect, we want
the waifus, we want the women

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:44.460
who do the stereotypical thing,

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:47.580
which is like kind of hide
behind your shone in king

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:49.680
and then, you know, battle, battle battle.

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:51.480
And maybe they're strong enough
too and you're like, cool.

00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:54.150
But, like, he's the one who's
going to do the final punch.

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:56.280
So I think it's also the way that we look

00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:59.850
at women in shonen, that is an issue.

00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:02.790
And Erza was a great combination.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.680
It's like, I'm gonna beat the big bad.

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:08.520
Nod to Gray. You guys sit
in the corner, I got this.

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:10.320
And that's what's great.

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:13.080
And I think a lot of people
were able to kind of accept that

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:14.670
a lot easier and it's something like that.

00:15:14.670 --> 00:15:16.800
But while, like you just said,

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:20.760
Makima is an incredibly written character,

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:23.730
yet you hate her and then in
most people's minds, like,

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:25.860
because I hate her, means
she's poorly written.

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:26.693
- Right.

00:15:26.693 --> 00:15:30.060
- Because we all want to
like and slash love a woman

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:31.320
in a shonen anime.

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.420
- Yeah, no. It's a false equivalency.

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:34.253
'Cause I do.

00:15:34.253 --> 00:15:37.170
I believe that if a
character is well written,

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:39.540
you hating them is not-
- Yeah.

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:41.580
- That isn't a bad thing.
It's still a commentary.

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:43.274
You have a strong opinion
- "Fullmetal Alchemist."

00:15:43.274 --> 00:15:44.467
Right?
- On someone.

00:15:44.467 --> 00:15:47.370
- "Fullmetal Alchemist" had Envy and Lust,

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:49.260
two incredibly written characters.

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:51.630
But it works, because you
knew that they were villains

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:52.463
from the beginning.

00:15:52.463 --> 00:15:54.780
- What's interesting about that
is I think that also applies

00:15:54.780 --> 00:15:58.320
not just to how women
are written in shonen,

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:01.530
but you know, as to people of color,

00:16:01.530 --> 00:16:04.080
that's also a big
conversation in this space

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:08.700
as more fans come in, about
that sort of representation.

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:11.130
And there's actually, there's
a YouTuber who I really like

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:13.680
called Blank Thoughts who has a series on-

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:14.640
- Yes, I know Blank Thoughts.

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:15.473
- Do you? Yeah.

00:16:15.473 --> 00:16:19.290
What it means to Be Black
in different series.

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:22.050
And he makes a very interesting point

00:16:22.050 --> 00:16:27.050
of we're not asking
for quote unquote black

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:29.340
or Latino representation
in the standpoint,

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:31.530
'cause when you give
what is a stereotypical

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:36.120
person of color character, you
get stereotypical characters.

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:40.530
It's just about having a
well-written character who happens

00:16:40.530 --> 00:16:42.120
to be a person of color.

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:43.670
And it refers the same way for a woman.

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:45.750
And I think in one of his videos,

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:46.890
one of the best examples he gives,

00:16:46.890 --> 00:16:51.150
which I fully agree with
is Yoruichi in "Bleach."

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:53.790
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
- She is an incredible

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:55.620
character and there isn't really anything

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:58.140
about her character or the
journey that she goes on

00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:01.080
that is so rooted in the fact

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:03.840
that she's a person of color or a woman.

00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:07.820
She's just an awesome character
and that's such a great way

00:17:07.820 --> 00:17:10.590
to insert representation.

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:12.870
His point is "Bleach" is one of the shonen

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:15.140
that does it the best,
'cause there are a lot

00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:16.350
of different people of color.

00:17:16.350 --> 00:17:19.890
Even from, just looking at
the main cast, you have Chad,

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:21.930
who's half Mexican and half Japanese,

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:24.525
and that is a part of his character.

00:17:24.525 --> 00:17:26.580
The discrimination that he
- Oh, wow. That's right.

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:30.960
suffers in that show has
made him such an outsider.

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:33.780
But he is an integral part of,

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:35.610
- Of this group. Yeah.
- As much of an integral part-

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:37.620
- As he can be within shonen.

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:40.530
- Yes, 'cause once you kind
of really start to bring in

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:43.770
the other shinigami and
stuff, the Karakura Town,

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:44.970
those characters go away.

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:47.100
Other than Orihime, they
go away a little bit.

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:49.230
- Yeah, of course, 'cause
she's got the almighty power

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:50.063
of turning back time.

00:17:50.063 --> 00:17:51.360
- Yes.

00:17:51.360 --> 00:17:54.713
But I think that applies
to people of color as well.

00:17:54.713 --> 00:17:55.950
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:58.080
- Just write a good character.

00:17:58.080 --> 00:17:59.820
- Who happens to be.

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:00.720
- And people will flock to them.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:01.923
- Yeah, exactly.

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:04.650
I mean, like, you look at "One Piece"

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:07.320
and it's like they don't
have ethnicities, really.

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:09.240
I mean, they're drawn
the way they're drawn,

00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:14.190
but until Oda put out
and said what ethnicity

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:17.850
they come from, then people
started really kind of claiming

00:18:17.850 --> 00:18:19.680
that person as their own and whatever.

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:22.080
But in all honesty, it's everywhere.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:24.600
And he takes inspiration from everywhere.

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:27.207
Brook is inspired off of "Flash."

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:31.260
At that point, what do you...

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:33.510
That's that character and it's dope.

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:36.060
- So what are in the vein of-

00:18:36.060 --> 00:18:38.010
Talking about representation
in shonen series,

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:40.560
what are some of the things
that you think shonen series

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:43.050
can improve on, other than representation?

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:44.070
We've covered that a little bit,

00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:45.660
but are there other
things that you're like,

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:47.280
okay, when I look at the genre,

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:48.960
are there things that are stale to you?

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:50.970
Are there things that you
think that it could do

00:18:50.970 --> 00:18:52.770
different or better?

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:54.030
- Of course.

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:56.310
I wouldn't call myself
the leading authority,

00:18:56.310 --> 00:18:57.143
and the things that I want.
- No, that's me.

00:18:57.143 --> 00:18:59.160
- Yeah, yeah, exactly. That's you.

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:01.872
The things that I would be interested in

00:19:01.872 --> 00:19:06.872
is more a reflection of
myself and where I am now.

00:19:07.590 --> 00:19:11.070
I would love to see more
thoughtful, dramatic storytelling.

00:19:11.070 --> 00:19:13.470
I would love to, like,
cry with these characters

00:19:13.470 --> 00:19:14.493
a little bit more.

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:18.480
And you have it in so many of
these series, like, you know,

00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:22.620
even rereading "Naruto"
when Guy Sensei opens

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:24.600
the Eighth Gate and he's like, you know,

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:25.650
we see his backstory.

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:26.940
Like, it makes you tear up.

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:28.920
And I love that and I want more of that,

00:19:28.920 --> 00:19:33.920
but I think I'm also more
partial and more sympathetic

00:19:34.470 --> 00:19:37.260
and understanding to those
things now that I'm 26 years old

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:40.590
and I want and I know and
I've experienced some version

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:44.640
of this while I have an
11-year-old little brother

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:49.050
and he's reading "One Piece"
for the very first time.

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:51.930
And I saw no tears out of
his eyes when, you know,

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:56.520
Nami is crying and he
puts the hat on things.

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:58.200
I mean, like, he's clearly emotional,

00:19:58.200 --> 00:20:01.020
but it's not fully set in for him.

00:20:01.020 --> 00:20:02.340
And I'm like, wow.

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:05.400
So to be honest, I don't want
anything to change in shonen.

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:08.100
I do. But that's my own selfishness.

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:11.970
And I think what they're doing
is great and the evolution

00:20:11.970 --> 00:20:13.950
that is already happening
with "Attack on Titan"

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:16.110
and "Jujutsu Kaisen" and,
you know, kind of the more

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:18.990
and "Chainsaw Man" and
how different and darker

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:22.200
the storytelling is going
is evident to the authors

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:24.540
growing up with their readers.

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:27.090
But I also want something for
the new generation to come

00:20:27.090 --> 00:20:31.710
and read again and be
laughing and crying too,

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:34.680
and be for their generation,
because again, at 11 years old,

00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:37.260
my little brother's not
watching "Chainsaw Man."

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:38.093
He's not.

00:20:38.093 --> 00:20:39.780
And so I don't want to alienate

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:41.520
the new generation that is coming.

00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:45.150
And of course, they have all
the material that we've had

00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:48.510
in our past to kind of read
and watch and whatever.

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:50.940
But yeah.

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:54.780
Again, selfishly, I would
love it to continue skewing

00:20:54.780 --> 00:20:58.050
more older and having
more dramatic moments,

00:20:58.050 --> 00:21:01.590
but at the same time, I'm
happy with where it's at.

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:05.250
And besides the representation,
which we've already said.

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:06.083
- Oh, you're right.

00:21:06.083 --> 00:21:08.940
And what's fun is I think we are seeing,

00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:11.183
'cause you're right, a lot
of creators, Kohei Horikoshi,

00:21:11.183 --> 00:21:14.340
Tatsuki Fujimoto, a lot
of these guys are like,

00:21:14.340 --> 00:21:16.020
they're our age.

00:21:16.020 --> 00:21:18.780
They came up with this stuff
and they're in their, you know,

00:21:18.780 --> 00:21:22.110
like, early 30s and they've lived,

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:24.330
they've experienced a lot of
the same things that we have.

00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:26.880
They have grown up with
a lot of the same content

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:28.860
that we have been consuming
and they're taking that

00:21:28.860 --> 00:21:30.180
to another level.

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:31.020
So I think you're right.

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:33.150
It's an interesting thing
to look at, you know,

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:36.090
when you have those
classic, like the big three

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:37.620
and things like that and to see

00:21:37.620 --> 00:21:38.910
where we've been moving into,

00:21:38.910 --> 00:21:40.290
I think there is an emotionality.

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:43.620
One of the things that I love the most

00:21:43.620 --> 00:21:48.620
about "My Hero Academia"
is Deku is an incredibly

00:21:48.930 --> 00:21:51.450
emotional character.
- Character. Exactly.

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:52.740
- He's prone to crying

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:54.420
and, like, sometimes they
make fun of him for that.

00:21:54.420 --> 00:21:58.470
But he is a character
who isn't afraid to feel

00:21:58.470 --> 00:22:00.240
and to show his emotions.

00:22:00.240 --> 00:22:02.490
And that's something that
I think is really nice

00:22:02.490 --> 00:22:04.140
to be giving to audiences.

00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:06.270
- 100%, one of the most emotional arcs

00:22:06.270 --> 00:22:08.820
in "One Piece" history in
my opinion, is Water 7.

00:22:08.820 --> 00:22:11.910
The moment where Usopp and
Luffy are fighting each other

00:22:11.910 --> 00:22:14.310
for The Going Merry.

